          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.085,
            0.879,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": "| First, we observe something that we find interestingor we do not understand. |\n| --- |\n| This makes us wonder and perhaps think of a questionabout it. |\n| Then, we guess a possible answer to that question. |\n| We test this guess through experiments or moreobservations. |\n| We then try to analyse the results to see if it actually answersour question. |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.531,
            0.377,
            0.884,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": "Scientists are people who follow the scientific method to solve problems or to discover new things. But anyone who follows the scientific method is working like a scientist. Someone cooking food may be wondering why the dal has spilled out of the cooker—was there too much water?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.532,
            0.574,
            0.884,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": "Think of a bicycle repair person trying to find out why a tyre is flat—from where did the air leak out? Or an electrician trying to find why a light bulb is not working—is there some problem with the bulb or the switch? When we try to ask questions and find out answers, we are all, in a way, scientists!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.785,
            0.631,
            0.808
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 1.2: Let us think and write"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.819,
            0.883,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": " Describe a daily life situation where you think someone was following a scientific method."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.865,
            0.883,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "Do you now realise that there are several daily-life situations where we knowingly or unknowingly apply the scientific"
